    "text": "Pakistan's current account swings to a $39 million surplus in October! 📊\nAccording to Business Recorder, State Bank of Pakistan (SBP) data released on Tuesday shows a current account surplus of $39 million in October 2026, compared with a deficit of $371 million in September and a deficit of $307 million in October last year. For the first four months of FY27, the current account deficit stood at $850 million, down from $1,062 million in the same period last year.\nIs Pakistan's economy finally on the right track? Tell us below 👇\n\nImage: AI-generated illustration.\n\n#RiseUpPakistan #SBP #CurrentAccount #PakistanEconomy #PakistanNews",
